{"condition_compatibility":"compatible","confidence":0.72,"content_digest":"6d592f94ca443549b9981dc447903f41fabb13c85ad18161cb6adcf1ebc0be62","created_at":"2026-08-22T03:25:50+00:00","direction":"principle_to_meta","generation_trace":[],"link_id":"foundation-link:03d96618e85c9ef89c55ee53","meta_principle_id":"meta:chemistry-materials:processing-structure-properties","meta_principle_revision":1,"principle_id":"prn:engineering-robotics:01M0F16KJ18SH4W5S69XWV54AR","principle_revision":1,"rationale":"The mobile-AM defect claim is a concrete instance of the processing-structure-properties chain: mechanical disturbance during processing introduces defects that alter structure and degrade adhesion/performance. The meta-principle provides the general materials-science framework, and the claim specializes it to mobile additive manufacturing under terrain-induced vibration.","relation_type":"specializes","review_attestation":{"actor":"principia-owner","basis":"Explicit Submit reviewed changeset confirmation in local Admin","reviewed_at":"2026-08-22T04:12:58+00:00","source_review_status":"unassessed","trace_id":"sync:01M0KTQZ6M68SKHPKARZR7EKFP"},"review_status":"reviewed","revision":1,"scale_compatibility":"compatible","schema_version":"global-foundation-link-v1","status":"active","updated_at":"2026-08-22T03:25:50+00:00","variable_compatibility":"compatible"}
{"condition_compatibility":"compatible","confidence":0.8,"content_digest":"ba5b42f67c95427e84071e9130a82fb422f8ff6661b69116bb6b8b72012a8c03","created_at":"2026-08-23T06:23:22+00:00","direction":"meta_to_principle","generation_trace":[{"attempts":1,"input_sha256":"8b85494eb45f0de14b06d2e338a7990a9bf28d81bb1763954da41dd3307edbca","input_tokens":5785,"latency_ms":27763,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash","output_sha256":"0c1ce48b57dedc4d1b375e884ba7c3ecd64c449385ee518522488d56faf12d99","output_tokens":2611,"prompt_sha256":"a0e24249a3438877119c33b7ce1b688152e1189df5765ebd53fae91f7c321069","prompt_template":"meta-grounding-v1","provider":"siliconflow","repair_attempted":false,"schema_valid":true,"transport_attempts":1}],"link_id":"foundation-link:95fed746d4c219b7b28b89f3","meta_principle_id":"meta:mathematics-logic:proof-model-distinction","meta_principle_revision":1,"principle_id":"prn:socio-technical-systems:01M0PMJMHT2VQTE3SN350AP5JE","principle_revision":1,"rationale":"The claim is a formal theorem about a toy model; the meta-principle correctly bounds its interpretation by distinguishing proof within the model from empirical adequacy of the model. This matches the principle's stated boundary that transfer beyond the toy model is unestablished.","relation_type":"bounded_by","review_attestation":{"actor":"principia-owner","basis":"Explicit Submit reviewed changeset confirmation in local Admin","reviewed_at":"2026-08-23T08:08:08+00:00","source_review_status":"unassessed","trace_id":"sync:01M0PTK9G6V6VXNVFWAWBHMSYT"},"review_status":"reviewed","revision":1,"scale_compatibility":"compatible","schema_version":"global-foundation-link-v1","status":"active","updated_at":"2026-08-23T06:23:22+00:00","variable_compatibility":"compatible"}
{"condition_compatibility":"compatible","confidence":0.75,"content_digest":"e1c33ff8ad1fb979a348bd0c4a30cbe27a06eefe55403e9ce9d4b0e4ebdd9e16","created_at":"2026-08-23T13:12:07+00:00","direction":"principle_to_meta","generation_trace":[{"attempts":1,"input_sha256":"dc5ed252bf28f8a811bb1153fd556950736d829bb40baf20baa2bd3b7eca81b1","input_tokens":5735,"latency_ms":38603,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash","output_sha256":"636600a665e09d255c97c2753f7fc9393f157e7b3d0fd0667757f3314347db6e","output_tokens":2553,"prompt_sha256":"a0e24249a3438877119c33b7ce1b688152e1189df5765ebd53fae91f7c321069","prompt_template":"meta-grounding-v1","provider":"siliconflow","repair_attempted":false,"schema_valid":true,"transport_attempts":1}],"link_id":"foundation-link:d1f4ca6369e9b5c33680617f","meta_principle_id":"meta:ai-ml:robustness-accuracy-tradeoff","meta_principle_revision":1,"principle_id":"prn:ai-ml:01M0QBYQGBNK8ERQQX8G9V1175","principle_revision":1,"rationale":"The principle reports that label smoothing improves adversarial robustness without generally improving classification accuracy, which is a concrete instance of the broader robustness-accuracy tradeoff: robust features can differ from those maximizing standard accuracy. The empirical observation is consistent with the meta-principle's claim that robustness and standard accuracy can conflict, though the principle does not establish the tradeoff itself.","relation_type":"consistent_with","review_attestation":{"actor":"principia-owner","basis":"Explicit Submit reviewed changeset confirmation in local Admin","reviewed_at":"2026-08-23T15:24:41+00:00","source_review_status":"unassessed","trace_id":"sync:01M0QKJMJD3A13DCG7YJ3ACW1G"},"review_status":"reviewed","revision":1,"scale_compatibility":"partial","schema_version":"global-foundation-link-v1","status":"active","updated_at":"2026-08-23T13:12:07+00:00","variable_compatibility":"compatible"}
{"condition_compatibility":"compatible","confidence":0.95,"content_digest":"2a3606446175337c6bc675e958802b56099a473b2709616092e14fa8e4b67178","created_at":"2026-08-22T03:25:37+00:00","direction":"meta_to_principle","generation_trace":[],"link_id":"foundation-link:e07641054eabd16b2f21be2d","meta_principle_id":"meta:computer-science:reduction-completeness","meta_principle_revision":1,"principle_id":"prn:interdisciplinary-science:01M0HEBPQF14V457KZG1MKK6BN","principle_revision":1,"rationale":"The weighted variant is shown NP-hard by a reduction from Subset Sum, a known NP-hard problem. The reduction-completeness meta-principle directly supports the hardness transfer: an efficient answer-preserving reduction from a hard problem makes the target problem at least as hard.","relation_type":"supports","review_attestation":{"actor":"principia-owner","basis":"Explicit Submit reviewed changeset confirmation in local Admin","reviewed_at":"2026-08-22T04:12:58+00:00","source_review_status":"unassessed","trace_id":"sync:01M0KTQZ6M68SKHPKARZR7EKFP"},"review_status":"reviewed","revision":1,"scale_compatibility":"compatible","schema_version":"global-foundation-link-v1","status":"active","updated_at":"2026-08-22T03:25:37+00:00","variable_compatibility":"compatible"}
